---
import BaseLayout from "../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
const updated = "2 November 2026";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Panorama — Privacy Policy"
  description="Privacy policy for Panorama, the location intelligence app by DataIsland Software LLC."
>

  <section class="legal fade-in">
    <div class="breadcrumb"><a href="/privacy">← All Privacy Policies</a></div>

    <h1>Panorama — Privacy Policy</h1>
    <p class="meta">DataIsland Software LLC &nbsp;·&nbsp; Last updated: {updated}</p>

    <p>
      Panorama is a location intelligence app for macOS and iPhone. This policy explains exactly
      what data Panorama collects, what leaves your device, and what is stored locally.
    </p>

    <h2>Summary</h2>
    <p>
      <strong>Panorama does not collect personal data.</strong> It has no account, no analytics
      and no advertising. Your saved locations, profiles and reports are stored only on your Mac.
      To fetch figures for a place, Panorama sends that place's name or coordinates to public data
      services; a few of those requests pass through a small DataIsland relay, described below,
      which forwards them and keeps nothing.
    </p>

    <h2>Location Searches</h2>
    <p>
      When you search for a place, Panorama sends what you type to OpenStreetMap's Nominatim
      geocoding service to find the place and its coordinates. Nominatim's own privacy policy
      governs that request.
    </p>

    <h2>Fetching Data for a Location</h2>
    <p>
      When you add or refresh a location, Panorama sends only what each data service needs —
      coordinates, a place or country name, a state or province code, or a county code — directly
      from your Mac to the services listed below. No personal information is included.
    </p>
    <p>
      Requests to a few US government services (the Census Bureau geocoder, FEMA hazard and flood
      data, EIA, BEA, and FBI and city police crime data) go through a relay that DataIsland runs on Cloudflare
      Workers, because those services often fail behind VPNs and network filters. The relay
      receives the same parameters (for example a location's coordinates for the flood-zone
      lookup), forwards the request, and returns the answer. It does not store requests or keep
      logs of them, and it cannot tell who you are. Cloudflare processes the traffic under its
      own privacy policy.
    </p>

    <h2>Saved Locations</h2>
    <p>
      Saved locations, the figures fetched for them, notes and AI summaries are stored locally
      on your Mac, in Panorama's own container. They are not uploaded to DataIsland or synced
      to any cloud service.
    </p>

    <h2>AI Summaries</h2>

    <h3>Apple Intelligence (on-device)</h3>
    <p>
      When you use Apple Intelligence, all processing happens on your Mac. No location data or
      profile content is sent to Apple or to DataIsland.
    </p>

    <h3>OpenRouter (optional cloud model)</h3>
    <p>
      If you choose to use OpenRouter, Panorama sends a summary of the location's figures (the
      assembled facts, not raw data) and your question to OpenRouter using your own OpenRouter
      key, which is stored in your macOS Keychain. OpenRouter's privacy policy and that of the
      model provider you select govern this. DataIsland does not receive it.
    </p>

    <h2>Data Services</h2>
    <p>
      Panorama fetches figures from the following public services. Each provider's privacy
      policy governs its handling of requests:
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li>US Census Bureau — census.gov</li>
      <li>FEMA (National Risk Index and flood zones, via Esri ArcGIS) — fema.gov</li>
      <li>CDC PLACES — cdc.gov</li>
      <li>FBI Crime Data Explorer — api.usa.gov</li>
      <li>City police open data (Socrata) — for 8 large US cities</li>
      <li>BEA — bea.gov</li>
      <li>BLS — bls.gov</li>
      <li>EIA — eia.gov</li>
      <li>USGS — earthquake.usgs.gov</li>
      <li>Statistics Canada — statcan.gc.ca</li>
      <li>UK police data — data.police.uk</li>
      <li>Eurostat — ec.europa.eu/eurostat</li>
      <li>World Bank — worldbank.org</li>
      <li>IMF — imf.org</li>
      <li>OECD — oecd.org</li>
      <li>WHO — who.int</li>
      <li>Open-Meteo (climate and air quality) — open-meteo.com</li>
      <li>Wikipedia — wikipedia.org</li>
      <li>Apple Maps (nearby places) — apple.com</li>
      <li>OpenStreetMap Nominatim (search) — openstreetmap.org</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Network Interference Detection</h2>
    <p>
      When a government service fails with a secure-connection error, Panorama may contact
      Cloudflare's trace endpoint (cloudflare.com/cdn-cgi/trace) to detect whether Cloudflare
      WARP is active, and Apple's egress list (mask-api.icloud.com) to detect iCloud Private
      Relay, so it can show you a specific fix. No personal data is included in these requests.
    </p>

    <h2>Crash Reports</h2>
    <p>
      Panorama uses Apple's MetricKit to keep crash and hang reports in a folder on your Mac so
      you can send them to us if you ask for support. Nothing is sent automatically. If you have
      chosen to share analytics with developers in macOS settings, Apple also provides anonymous
      crash reports to DataIsland through App Store Connect.
    </p>

    <h2>What Panorama Does Not Do</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Does not send your searches or saved locations to DataIsland</li>
      <li>Does not keep any record of requests on the relay</li>
      <li>Does not require an account or login</li>
      <li>Does not use advertising SDKs or share data with advertisers</li>
      <li>Does not collect analytics or usage statistics</li>
      <li>Does not read or transmit your contacts, photos, or other personal files</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Children's Privacy</h2>
    <p>
      Panorama is not directed at children under 13. We do not knowingly collect information
      from children.
    </p>

    <h2>Changes to This Policy</h2>
    <p>
      If we make material changes to this policy, we will update the "Last updated" date above.
      Continued use of Panorama after changes constitutes acceptance of the updated policy.
    </p>

    <h2>Contact</h2>
    <p>
      Questions about this policy:
      <br />
      <a href="mailto:support@dataisland.com">support@dataisland.com</a>
      <br />
      DataIsland Software LLC
    </p>
  </section>

</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .legal {
    max-width: 800px;
    margin: 0 auto;
    padding: 3rem 0 5rem;
    border-bottom: none;
  }

  .breadcrumb { margin-bottom: 2rem; font-size: 0.9rem; }
  .legal h1 { font-size: 2.1rem; margin-bottom: 0.5rem; }
  .meta { font-size: 0.9rem; color: var(--gray); margin-bottom: 2rem; }
  .legal h2 { margin-top: 2.25rem; margin-bottom: 0.6rem; font-size: 1.2rem; }
  .legal h3 { margin-top: 1.5rem; margin-bottom: 0.5rem; font-size: 1rem; font-weight: 600; }
  .legal p  { font-size: 1rem; line-height: 1.7; margin-bottom: 0.9rem; }

  ul { margin: 0.5rem 0 1rem 1.25rem; color: var(--gray-dark); }
  ul li { margin-bottom: 0.4rem; font-size: 0.97rem; line-height: 1.5; }
</style>
